  description="Professional website of Amirhossein Eskorouchi, a Machine Learning and Optimization Researcher and Ph.D. Candidate in Industrial and Systems Engineering at Mississippi State University."
>
  <section class="home-intro">
    <div class="home-copy">
      <h1>Hi there, I’m Amirhossein Eskorouchi!</h1>

      <p class="home-lead">
        I am a <strong>Machine Learning and Optimization Researcher</strong>{" "}
        with more than four years of experience developing AI methods and
        intelligent decision systems. I am also an{" "}
        <strong>Industrial and Systems Engineering (ISE) Ph.D. Candidate</strong>{" "}
        at Mississippi State University (MSU), where I am fortunate to conduct
        my doctoral research under the guidance of{" "}
        <a
          href="https://eng.auburn.edu/directory/haw0079"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          Dr. Haifeng Wang
        </a>{" "}
        and{" "}
        <a
          href="https://www.ise.msstate.edu/people/faculty/mohammad-marufuzzaman/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          Dr. Mohammad Marufuzzaman
        </a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        My research focuses on developing reliable and decision-relevant
        artificial intelligence. I specialize in computer vision and
        optimization-guided learning, integrating domain knowledge, physical
        constraints, and mathematical optimization into machine learning to
        improve model reliability, interpretability, and generalizability under
        limited and heterogeneous data. I apply these methods to real-world
        decision problems in healthcare, intelligent manufacturing, and smart
        agriculture.
      </p>

      <p>
        My work spans the complete research and development lifecycle, from
        problem formulation and algorithm design to large-scale experimentation,
        rigorous validation, research dataset development, reproducible
        software, and deployment-oriented prototyping. My goal is to translate
        methodological advances into practical intelligent systems that support
        better decisions in complex scientific and engineering environments.
      </p>

      <p>
        Through interdisciplinary collaborations in industrial and systems
        engineering, sustainable bioproducts, radiation oncology, and biomedical
        research, I have contributed to projects supported by USDA-NIFA, NIH,
        and the Mississippi Institutions of Higher Learning. Alongside my
        research, I mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers and contribute
        to engineering education, research leadership, and professional service.
      </p>

